public with sharing class ContactLookupAction {

    public class Request {
        @InvocableVariable(required=true label='Email' description='Contact email to search for')
        public String email;
    }

    public class Result {
        @InvocableVariable(label='Contact Id' description='Id of the matching contact, if found')
        public Id contactId;

        @InvocableVariable(label='Found' description='True if a contact with this email exists')
        public Boolean found;
    }

    @InvocableMethod(label='Find Contact by Email' description='Finds an existing contact by email address')
    public static List<Result> find(List<Request> requests) {
        List<Result> results = new List<Result>();
        Set<String> emails = new Set<String>();

        for (Request req : requests) {
            if (req != null && req.email != null && req.email.trim() != '') {
                emails.add(req.email.trim().toLowerCase());
            }
        }

        Map<String, Id> emailToContactId = new Map<String, Id>();
        if (!emails.isEmpty()) {
            for (Contact c : [
                SELECT Email, CreatedDate
                FROM Contact
                WHERE Email != null
                ORDER BY CreatedDate ASC
            ]) {
                String key = c.Email.trim().toLowerCase();
                if (emails.contains(key) && !emailToContactId.containsKey(key)) {
                    emailToContactId.put(key, c.Id);
                }
            }
        }

        for (Request req : requests) {
            Result res = new Result();
            res.contactId = null;
            res.found = false;
            if (req != null && req.email != null && req.email.trim() != '') {
                Id contactId = emailToContactId.get(req.email.trim().toLowerCase());
                if (contactId != null) {
                    res.contactId = contactId;
                    res.found = true;
                }
            }
            results.add(res);
        }
        return results;
    }
}
```

Notes on the implementation:

- **One SOQL query per call**: all emails are collected into a set, then a single query (ordered by `CreatedDate ASC`) retrieves candidates. The first contact encountered per normalized email is the earliest-created one, satisfying the tie-break rule.
- **Normalization**: input emails are trimmed and lowercased; contact emails are normalized the same way for case-insensitive matching.
- **Blank/null handling**: those requests short-circuit to `found = false`, `contactId = null`, but still produce a `Result` in order.
- **Order preserved**: results are built in the same iteration order as the requests (one per request, per Flow invocable Apex contract).
- **Sharing**: `with sharing` ensures the running user's record visibility is respected, so contacts outside their access are never returned.

