public with sharing class ContactPhoneCleanup {

    public static Map<Id, String> normalizePhones(List<Id> contactIds) {
        Map<Id, String> errors = new Map<Id, String>();

        if (contactIds == null || contactIds.isEmpty()) {
            return errors;
        }

        List<Contact> contacts = [
            SELECT Id, Phone
            FROM Contact
            WHERE Id IN :contactIds
        ];

        List<Contact> toUpdate = new List<Contact>();
        for (Contact c : contacts) {
            if (String.isNotBlank(c.Phone)) {
                String normalized = c.Phone.replaceAll('[^0-9+]', '');
                if (normalized != c.Phone) {
                    c.Phone = normalized;
                    toUpdate.add(c);
                }
            }
        }

        if (toUpdate.isEmpty()) {
            return errors;
        }

        List<Database.SaveResult> results = Database.update(toUpdate, false);
        for (Integer i = 0; i < results.size(); i++) {
            if (!results[i].isSuccess()) {
                errors.put(toUpdate[i].Id, results[i].getErrors()[0].getMessage());
            }
        }
        return errors;
    }
}
```

**Changes I made to your approach, and why:**

1. **Query only the needed fields (`SELECT Id, Phone`)** rather than updating whatever was passed in. Your signature takes `List<Id>`, so the method has to query the contacts anyway; selecting just `Phone` (and `Id`, required) keeps the query lean and makes the DML update only the `Phone` field, which avoids overwriting other fields with stale values.

